    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d47-a3">

                <pb facs="0110" n="76" xml:id="pg76"/>

                <head>Mr. Fish to Mr. E. B. Washburne.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[By cable.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 17, 1870</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washburne,</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Paris</hi>:</p>
                <p>Government and people of the United States depend upon German steamers between
                    Bremen, Hamburg, and New York for postal communication with Europe, under
                    arrangements with the United States Post Office. Inquire whether, in the event
                    of war with North Germany, these steamers will be exempt from capture. Report by
                    cable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
